<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fréjus</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Forum Julii</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fréjus is a town in the Var <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast. It began as Forum Julii, a market town founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> or his heir, and under Augustus it became a Roman colony and naval base where ships captured at Actium were stationed. Its Roman amphitheatre, aqueduct and early Christian baptistery survive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frejus.jpg" alt="Fréjus" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cyrilb1881 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MairieFr%C3%A9jus.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
